<title>POLAND: Polish cinema firm wants 20 pct of market in 2000.</title>
<headline>Polish cinema firm wants 20 pct of market in 2000.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish firm  Multikino Sp. z o.o. wants to gain 20 percent of the cinema market in Poland by 2000 thanks to its $70 million programme of building multi-screen cinemas, a deputy president of the firm said.</p>
<p>The investment programme of Multikino, which is equally owned by the Luxembourg-based Polish firm ITI Holdings SA and United Cinema International (UCI), envisages building 10 multi-screen cinemas in Poland.</p>
<p>&quot;We are starting with building cinemas in Warsaw and Poznan this year...we believe we will have 20 percent of the market in the year 2000,&quot; Aldona Szostakowska told Reuters.</p>
<p>-- Malgorzata Rzepka +48 22 653 9700</p>
